# RMAN configuration for orcl3 (run once: rman target / cmdfile=\"01-strategy/configure.rman\")
# The path must be quoted: unquoted, RMAN parses the leading "01" as an integer (RMAN-01009),
# both with @file and with cmdfile=file.
# /u02/backup is on the root disk (vda), not on the datafile disk (vdb): losing one disk must not
# lose both the datafiles and their backups. Created by root, owned by oracle.
# - recovery window instead of redundancy: "can I restore to any point of the last 7 days?"
# - BASIC compression is included in Enterprise Edition; LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH need the Advanced Compression Option
# - backups go to /u02/backup (outside the FRA, which already holds redo, archived and flashback logs)
CONFIGURE RETENTION POLICY TO RECOVERY WINDOW OF 7 DAYS;
CONFIGURE BACKUP OPTIMIZATION ON;
CONFIGURE CONTROLFILE AUTOBACKUP ON;
CONFIGURE CONTROLFILE AUTOBACKUP FORMAT FOR DEVICE TYPE DISK TO '/u02/backup/orcl3/cf_%F';
CONFIGURE DEVICE TYPE DISK PARALLELISM 2 BACKUP TYPE TO COMPRESSED BACKUPSET;
CONFIGURE COMPRESSION ALGORITHM 'BASIC';
CONFIGURE CHANNEL DEVICE TYPE DISK FORMAT '/u02/backup/orcl3/%d_%T_%U';
# Logs may be deleted only when applied on the standby AND backed up once: with just
# 'APPLIED ON ALL STANDBY' the 10-minute housekeeping job could delete a log before the next
# backup, leaving a gap that makes point-in-time recovery into that window impossible.
CONFIGURE ARCHIVELOG DELETION POLICY TO APPLIED ON ALL STANDBY BACKED UP 1 TIMES TO DEVICE TYPE DISK;
SHOW ALL;
